        state: "live",
        what: "Built 2026-11-26 (the cybernetic pass). At the top of the Devices window stands the ALL-STOP: one switch, yours alone, that halts EVERY device command. Engage it and the state reads STOPPED in plain words — from that moment every send is refused twice over: the send engine refuses before anything touches a wire, and the bridge on the core checks the halt again on every request it serves, so there is no road around it. Release it and the state reads Live — sends may go again, each still under its own Permission Law grant. Every engage and every release is written into the device command log with its time, so the record shows when the stop stood. Anubis has no road to this switch at all — he cannot engage it, and he cannot release it; his capability brief tells him plainly when it stands, so he will not offer to send what you have halted. Under the switch, THE LAW IN FORCE: the Permission Law's standing, counted from the registry at the moment you look — how many devices are registered, how many carry your control grant, how many stand under NO CONTROL, and how many flag requests wait for your hand. The counts are counted fresh every time, never stored, so they can never drift from the cards themselves.",
