        what: "Built 2026-11-26 (the cybernetic pass). One core, one memory, one command — and more than one surface reaching it: the Parrot, this screen, the online copy, the Osiris node, the phone. The Formation is the board where they all stand together. Open Settings → Connections — APIs & data → “The Formation — every surface of the one core.” Every row is PROBED when the board opens, and again when you press “Probe again” — nothing on it is a remembered state dressed as live. THE PARROT CORE: REACHED when the core link's own probe is answered just now; otherwise its true link state, in words. THIS SURFACE: the copy you are looking at, with the build stamp its own server reports. THE ONLINE COPY: from any other surface, no honest probe can read the build it is serving — the row says NO LIVE READING and tells you to open the online copy's own board; when you ARE on the online copy, its row is this surface's own reading. THE OSIRIS NODE: knocked on its own address, 10.42.0.1 — REACHED when something answers; UNREACHED reports the knock, not a verdict on the node (it may be off, out of this surface's reach, or the browser may refuse the knock). THE PHONE COPY: NO LIVE READING from here — no surface can read another's link state; its own board, on the phone, carries its reading. Under the rows, THE PARITY LINE in plain words: whether this surface carries the newest build, or is BEHIND it — because a fix that lives on only one copy is not done. And the LIVE SENSES census: what the core's senses have on record, counted at the moment you look — sounds classified, alerts waiting, devices registered and present, and whether the signal watcher is reporting. The Go Drive is deliberately NOT a row: it is not a network surface. Its truth is the Seal Check (see Offline & the Go Drive).",
