        what: "Pulse (Senses & analysis) reads heart rate from the phone or computer camera — an ESTIMATE, never a medical reading. The picture stands big in the middle now, with heart rate on its left and the room's frequencies on its right, and the live summary line inside the picture in a dark corner box whose size never changes, so the screen never jumps when a number updates. The estimate is tightened the way watch firmware works, at camera scale: three skin patches (forehead and both cheeks) are combined, the signal is filtered to the heart band, frames where motion swamps the signal are thrown out, and a number is shown only once recent estimates agree with each other — with the live signal-quality percentage beside it. SEARCHING with a climbing quality % means it is hearing the signal but will not print a number until the readings agree. It cannot do what a watch's skin-contact sensor does: room light, stillness, and a plain view of the face decide what the camera can honestly read, and when the signal is not there it stays SEARCHING instead of inventing a number. Nothing is recorded or stored, and no face is identified — presence and pulse only.",
